From: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@fyralabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: restore TG5050 panel reset and initialization

The generic pro3 board only sends sleep-out/display-on and has no reset
GPIO. Timing correction alone can inherit U-Boot scanout but cannot
reinitialize the panel after power-down or a warm restart.

Restore PD22, the 120 ms reset delay, and all 28 initialization commands
from the shipping TG5050 kernel DTB. Preserve the vendor driver's physical
low/high reset semantics (GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH), rather than inverting them.
The existing panel prepare callback executes this sequence after reset;
no blanket display-engine force flush is needed for this board fix.

Reference: mkosi.profiles/tg5050/board/boot-artifacts/vendor-kernel.dtb
SHA256: 8226f3805d991cc3dda31e621190844b4e338fb6bb28402ecd17b97524af5f9f
Only the kernel GPIO binding is copied, not U-Boot's vendor cell format.
Physical warm-reboot and suspend/resume validation remains required.

--- a/configs/pro3_linux_aiot/linux-5.15/board.dts
+++ b/configs/pro3_linux_aiot/linux-5.15/board.dts
@@ -171,7 +171,9 @@
 		status = "okay";
 		reg = <0>;
 		reset-num = <1>;
-		reset-delay-ms = <20>;
+		reset-delay-ms = <120>;
+		/* The vendor driver pulses physical low, then high. */
+		reset-gpios = <&pio PD 22 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		power0-supply = <&reg_cldo4>;
 		power1-supply = <&reg_cldo1>;
 		backlight = <&backlight0>;
@@ -180,8 +182,34 @@
 		dsi,lanes = <4>;
 		dsi,format = <0>;
 		panel-init-sequence = [
